areer. Meanwhile, Julia, who made her feature film debut in 1988, quickly surpassed her brother's fame after earning Academy Award nominations in back-to-back years for her work in Steel Magnolias (Best Supporting Actress) and Pretty Woman (Best Actress). Julia appeared in a number of blockbuster films throughout the 1990s, and"
