    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Celebrities Who Married The Same Person Twice\nauthor: Stassi Reid\ndate: 2018-12-31\n---\nCelebrities Who Married The Same Person Twice\n\n\"Until death do us part\" \u2014 It's perhaps the most famous line from traditional marriage vows, and yet, for most Hollywood marriages anyway, that seems to be the exception to the rule. Most stars are lucky to make it to their 10 year anniversary, leaving Tinseltown to be known for its barrage of quickie marriages and even more dramatic divorces. But a few of Hollywood's most influential stars didn't let their divorce decrees stop them from finding love again \u2014 and they didn't have to look too far to find their next mate. They simply fell back in love with someone they had already married and divorced in the past!\n\nFor some of these stars, their marriage re-dos have panned out quite nicely, while others haven't been so lucky. They either ran into the same issues that split them up the first time around, or, sadly, they were separated by death. Pamela Anderson, Marie Osmond, and Eminem remarried their exes, and they aren't the only ones who decided to walk down the aisle with an ex-spouse. Here are the stories of love, divorce, and reconciliation from celebrities who've married the same person twice.\n\nAt least Barbara Walters was left with a lavish apartment\n\nBarbara Walters and the late Merv Adelson appeared to be the perfect pairing when they tied the knot in 1981. She was a well-respected television personality, and he was a producer and the co-founder of Lorimar Television. What could possibly go wrong? We're not too sure, but CBS Los Angeles noted the couple called it quits just three years later, in 1984.\n\nHowever, they couldn't keep their paws off of each other for long. By the time May 1986 rolled around, the duo was ready to give love another shot. According to Variety, they invited \"about 30 guests\" to their 1986 Bel-Air, Calif. wedding, but \"more than 100 people\" showed up to celebrate the smitten couple. One guest called it a \"fabulous night,\" but it's just too bad it wouldn't last... again.\n\nWalters is used to being the one who asks all the questions, but she did give a rare interview with the New York Times in 1992, just before she divorced Adelson a second time"
